as promised a work-in-progress version  of the first fallout 4 patch has arrived  Bethesda released update version 1.2  point 33 today which is available for  players on PC who have opted in to  receive beta updates the patch  introduces a few new features for  instance the number pad keys are now  available free mapping and the quick  container can be used with remapping  activate and as always there are a  handful of bug fixes and general  stability improvements specifically the  team fixed a crash related to jumping  into water and reloading saved games  Bethesda cautions that this fallout 4  update is non final and suggest you  backup your saved games before opting  into the beta you can do that by  right-clicking the game in your library  go to properties and then betas you can  drop out of the beta at any time in the  same menu last week Bethesda said it was  hard at work addressing the top issues  patches will be released in beta on  Steam first followed by a full release  on PC before finally coming to consoles  generally speaking fallout 4 players can  also look forward to smaller and more  frequent updates rather than a few major  ones no timetable was provided regarding  when this fallout 4 patch will be  released to the world at large but we'll  have that information for you as it's  announced
 

